I am standing on the platform.
I am waiting for the U-Bahn.
A man comes over to me.
He has a large map in his hand.
"Excuse me," the man says.
"Can you please help me?"
"Of course, gladly," I answer.
"I am looking for the Pergamon Museum," he explains.
I smile and look at his map.
I point to a stop on the map.
"That is quite easy," I say.
"You take the next U-Bahn here."
"You ride for three stops."
"Then you get out."
The man is happy.
"Thank you very much for your help!" he says.
"You're welcome," I answer.
The U-Bahn arrives.
The man boards and waves.
